From 81fe59fab71aa40a1d9ae4946dec5a96d405e10d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:42:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 118/120] gpu: larger emulated EDRAM (gpu_edram_tiles) and
 keep-aspect pixel shaders from the DS2 port

Engine-independent renderer pieces of the Dark Souls II port's SDK (its commits 60975d3,
e10e98d, 6f4a86f / 638e553); defaults leave LR's behaviour unchanged.

- gpu_edram_tiles (init-only, 2048 default; 4096 / 8192, host render targets path only): the
  render target cache's EDRAM tile address space (xenos::EdramTileCount(), set by
  RenderTargetCache::ApplyEdramTileCountConfig), so surfaces a title places beyond the console's
  10 MiB (a 1920x1080 screen) do not alias. Bases come from RB_COLOR_INFO / RB_DEPTH_INFO
  base_tiles() (bits 0-11 / 0-12); render target, framebuffer, transfer and dump keys/constants
  widened to 13-bit bases; ResolveInfo carries the whole-EDRAM bases. The EDRAM buffer, the
  resolve shaders and one render target keep the console's 2048-tile period: render target
  heights round down and owned lengths are capped at 2048 tiles when extended (DS2 e10e98d:
  device loss and wrapped resolves at 1080p). ApplyEdramTileCountConfig runs after the last
  path switch of VulkanRenderTargetCache::Initialize (the bit-exact transfer fallback to the
  fragment shader interlock), not before it as in DS2.
- gpu_keep_aspect_pixel_shaders (hex hashes, comma-separated, empty default) and
  gpu_keep_aspect_pillarbox (off): those pixel shaders' draws keep a 16:9 picture when their
  viewport is wider (a movie player on a wide screen): NDC Y scaled about the centre by
  W*9/(16*H), or a centred 16:9 viewport with the pillarbox switch.

Left out: DS2's redirected MSAA-alias depth clear bounds (LR has no redirected clears),
vulkan_skip_no_effect_draws and the game-side render size hooks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

